<title>USA: Mercom sells Fla. cable system.</title>
<headline>Mercom sells Fla. cable system.</headline>
<dateline>PRINCETON, N.J. 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mercom Inc said it has agreed to sell its cable system in Port St. Lucie, Fla., to Adelphia Communications Corp for $3.75 million.</p>
<p>The cable system has 1,875 subscribers.</p>
<p>&quot;This sale makes sense because it allows us to focus on growing Mercom's core subscriber base in Michigan and further upgrading our services there,&quot; Mercom Chairman and Chief Executive David McCourt said in a statement.</p>
<p>Adelphia already has its own subscriber base in Port St. Lucie.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
